{"id":"0cd6f9d4f0451efa","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-df-zfc-metric-uniformly-continuous-map.md","title":"ZFC Metric Uniformly Continuous Map","display":"df-zfc-metric-uniformly-continuous-map — ZFC Metric Uniformly Continuous Map","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-metric-uniformly-continuous-map","aliases":["58-df-zfc-metric-uniformly-continuous-map"],"display":"df-zfc-metric-uniformly-continuous-map — ZFC Metric Uniformly Continuous Map","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[58-df-function]]","[[58-df-metric]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-metric-uniformly-continuous-map"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-metric-uniformly-continuous-map</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-metric-uniformly-continuous-map — ZFC Metric Uniformly Continuous Map"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"267957a097ff75bf\" href=\"?note=267957a097ff75bf\" title=\"58-df-metric\">58-df-metric</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,Y,f,d_X,d_Y,\\epsilon,\\delta\\in V\">\\(X,Y,f,d_X,d_Y,\\epsilon,\\delta\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Metric}_S:V^2\\to\\mathsf{Bool}\">\\(\\mathrm{Metric}_S:V^2\\to\\mathsf{Bool}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"267957a097ff75bf\" href=\"?note=267957a097ff75bf\" title=\"58-df-metric\">58-df-metric</a>) and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\mathsf{Bool}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\mathsf{Bool}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMetricUniformlyContinuousMap}_S:V^5\\to\\mathsf{Bool}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMetricUniformlyContinuousMap}_S:V^5\\to\\mathsf{Bool}\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}metric\\text{-}uniformly\\text{-}continuous\\text{-}map}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcMetricUniformlyContinuousMap}_S(f,X,Y,d_X,d_Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Metric}_S(d_X,X)\n\\land\\mathrm{Metric}_S(d_Y,Y)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(f,X,Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall\\epsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\Bigl(\nd_X(\\langle x,y\\rangle)&lt;\\delta\n\\to d_Y(\\langle f(x),f(y)\\rangle)&lt;\\epsilon\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}metric\\text{-}uniformly\\text{-}continuous\\text{-}map}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcMetricUniformlyContinuousMap}_S(f,X,Y,d_X,d_Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Metric}_S(d_X,X)\n\\land\\mathrm{Metric}_S(d_Y,Y)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(f,X,Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall\\epsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\Bigl(\nd_X(\\langle x,y\\rangle)&lt;\\delta\n\\to d_Y(\\langle f(x),f(y)\\rangle)&lt;\\epsilon\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Both distances are applied to ordered pairs, exactly as required by the registered metric signature.  The two positive-real quantifier domains are explicit.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-zfc]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-metric","status":"resolved","id":"267957a097ff75bf","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-metric]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-metric","status":"resolved","id":"267957a097ff75bf","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Metric}_S:V^2\\to\\mathsf{Bool}$ (see [[58-df-metric]]) and $\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\mathsf{Bool}$ (see [[58-df-function]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Metric}_S:V^2\\to\\mathsf{Bool}$ (see [[58-df-metric]]) and $\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\mathsf{Bool}$ (see [[58-df-function]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,Y,f,d_X,d_Y,\\epsilon,\\delta\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Metric}_S:V^2\\to\\mathsf{Bool}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\mathsf{Bool}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcMetricUniformlyContinuousMap}_S:V^5\\to\\mathsf{Bool}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}metric\\text{-}uniformly\\text{-}continuous\\text{-}map}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcMetricUniformlyContinuousMap}_S(f,X,Y,d_X,d_Y)\\\\\n&\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Metric}_S(d_X,X)\n\\land\\mathrm{Metric}_S(d_Y,Y)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(f,X,Y)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land\\forall\\epsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\n\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\Bigl(\nd_X(\\langle x,y\\rangle)<\\delta\n\\to d_Y(\\langle f(x),f(y)\\rangle)<\\epsilon\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":1363,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-2695","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-zfc-metric-uniformly-continuous-map.md|58-df-zfc-metric-uniformly-continuous-map]]（batch03）"}],"outgoing":["a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","36d7463d215be751","267957a097ff75bf"]}